HSE/PSM/F/01 Technical Specification
1. MOC Header (Metadata)
•	MOC ID: Auto-generated
•	MOC Type: Enum [Permanent, Temporary]
•	Department: String
•	Plant/Section: String
•	Date of Initiation: Date
•	MOC Coordinator: String
•	Date of Closure: Date (Nullable)
2. Change Category (Multi-select)
•	Raw Material | Safety Interlock | Facility Layout | Equipment/Instrument
•	SIF/SIS/SIL | Vendor Format Spec | New Product Process | Packing Material
•	Software Modification
3. Description & Justification
•	Description of Change: Textarea (Rich text)
•	Reason/Justification: Textarea (Rich text)
4. Cost Matrix (Table)
•	Rows: [Description of Change, Cost In Lacs, Initiator Sign, Date]
5. Required Approvals (Dynamic Checkbox Logic)
•	Departments: [QA-QC, Instrument, Civil, Utility, Production, Mechanical, Electrical, Purchase, Tech Services]
•	Logic: Selecting a department here triggers an entry in the ApprovalStep table.
6. Attachments & Checklist
•	Checklist items: [HSE Initial Evaluation, SHE Checklist, Hazop Study/RA Sheet, PFD/P&ID, Other]
•	P&ID Updatation Target Date: Date
7. Approval Workflow (Sign-off Matrix)
•	Departments requiring sign-off: Process, Tech Serv, Engineering, Utility, Commercial, QA-QC, Others.
•	Fields per row: [Comments, Signature, Date]
8. Final Authorization
•	Required Signatories: [Head Production, Head Engineering, Head EHS, Unit Head]

### Why this structure works:
* **The "Sections" map to your DB:
** `Section 1` becomes your `MOC_Request` table. `Section 4` becomes your `CostMatrix` table. `Section 5 & 7` become your `ApprovalStep` table.
* **Cursor Integration:** When you start Phase 3 (UI), you can tell Cursor: *"Build the MOC intake form using the fields and hierarchy defined in `/docs/hse_psm_f01_spec.md`."* 